  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to put to use, to make use of",
      "explanation": "To utilize something effectively for a particular purpose. Implies actively making something serve a useful function."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "12550_yakudateru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{経験|けいけん}を{役立|やくだ}てる。",
      "english": "To put one's experience to use.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "12550_yakudateru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{留学|りゅうがく}で{学|まな}んだことを{仕事|しごと}に{役立|やくだ}てたい。",
      "english": "I want to put what I learned while studying abroad to use in my work.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "12550_yakudateru_ex3",
      "japanese": "この{本|ほん}の{知識|ちしき}を{日常|にちじょう}{生活|せいかつ}に{役立|やくだ}てることができる。",
      "english": "You can put the knowledge from this book to use in everyday life.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "USAGE:\n{役立|やくだ}てる is transitive — someone actively puts something to use. Compare with the intransitive {役立|やくだ}つ, which means something is useful on its own. {役立|やくだ}てる emphasizes the agent's intentional use of a resource.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {経験|けいけん}を{役立|やくだ}てる: to put experience to use\n- {知識|ちしき}を{役立|やくだ}てる: to put knowledge to use\n- {仕事|しごと}に{役立|やくだ}てる: to put to use in one's work\n- {社会|しゃかい}に{役立|やくだ}てる: to put to use for society",
